From: MythologyKombat local launcher patch set (D19, T3.12)
Subject: [PATCH 0003] GAME card: wrap long values (the disc file name) instead of clipping

Issue (design item 3; work/screens/shot_230017.png): the File row shows
  "Mortal Kombat Mythologies - Sub-Zero.c" and the rest is cut at the cell
  edge, because kv_row draws the value with TextUnformatted (no wrap).

Fix: kv_row wraps the value at the column edge (PushTextWrapPos(0)). Nothing is
  lost and no hover is needed (a gamepad user cannot hover). Short values
  (Serial, Region) draw exactly as before. Wrap was chosen over an ellipsis with
  a tooltip for that reason.

Verified: yes (framebuffer captures, work/screens/).
Upstream candidate: yes (4 lines, low risk).
---
diff --git a/src/common/backends/imgui/launcher_imgui.cpp b/src/common/backends/imgui/launcher_imgui.cpp
index 8ba5731..2e6eb73 100644
--- a/src/common/backends/imgui/launcher_imgui.cpp
+++ b/src/common/backends/imgui/launcher_imgui.cpp
@@ -1804,7 +1804,11 @@ void kv_row(const char* k, const char* v, const LauncherTheme& th,
     ImGui::TextUnformatted(ui_text(k));
     ImGui::PopStyleColor();
     ImGui::TableNextColumn();
+    // Wrap at the column edge: a long value (a disc file name) used to be cut
+    // off mid-word by the cell clip.
+    ImGui::PushTextWrapPos(0.0f);
     ImGui::TextUnformatted(v);
+    ImGui::PopTextWrapPos();
     ImGui::TableNextColumn();
     if (show_mark) state_mark(ok, th);
 }
